name \"*.cfg\" 2>/dev/null | head -20","description":"Find all configuration files"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EjyZtkqKNxD8jTh7yxWrGD","tool_input":{"command":"ls -lh /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow/data/20130502/*.vcf 2>/dev/null | head","description":"Check for VCF files in data directory"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01XHAh2e3pb1nsteGZqopkuh","tool_input":{"file_path":"/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial3.md","content":"# Workflow Knowledge Report: 1000 Genomes\n\n**Workflow**: 1000genome\n**Agent**: claude\n**Date**: 2026-03-04\n**Source**: Static analysis of `/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow`\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Repository Survey\n\n### Entry Points and Structure\n\n```\n1000genome-workflow/\n├── daxgen.py              # Main workflow generator (Pegasus DAX/YAML)\n├── data.csv               # Input manifest: 10 chromosomes × VCF + SIFT annotation paths\n├── prepare_input.sh       # Downloads/unzips raw input data (not part of workflow logic)\n├── env.sh                 # Environment setup for Decaf in-memory execution (deployment only)\n├── ares_1kgenome_parallel.sbatch  # HPC batch submission script\n├── bin/\n│   ├── individuals.py     # Task: parse VCF and extract per-individual mutations\n│   ├── individuals_merge.py  # Task: merge parallel individual chunks\n│   ├── sifting.py         # Task: extract SIFT functional annotation scores\n│   ├── mutation_overlap.py   # Task: pairwise overlap analysis + visualization\n│   └── frequency.py       # Task: bootstrap mutation frequency estimation\n├── data/\n│   ├── 20130502/          # Input VCF and SIFT annotation files\n│   │   ├── chr1n/         # Sample individual-level files\n│   │   ├── sifting/       # SIFT annotation VCFs\n│   │   └── columns.txt    # 2504 individual IDs (column headers)\n│   └── populations/       # Population membership files: AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS\n└── analysis/              # Post-hoc analysis scripts (not part of core workflow)\n```\n\n**Orchestration**: `daxgen.py` generates a Pegasus workflow DAX (YAML format) that defines all tasks, file dependencies, and execution sites. The workflow engine drives task scheduling.\n\n**Key Configuration File**: `data.csv` lists one row per chromosome: `filename, num_rows, sift_file`.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Stages and Tasks\n\n### Stage Grouping\n\n| Stage ID | Stage Name       | Tasks                                 | Description |\n|----------|-----------------|---------------------------------------|-------------|\n| stage:individuals | Individuals Extraction | individuals | Parse VCF files to extract per-individual SNP mutations |\n| stage:merge | Individuals Merge | individuals_merge | Merge parallel per-chromosome chunks |\n| stage:sifting | SIFT Annotation | sifting | Extract functional effect predictions from annotation VCF |\n| stage:analysis | Overlap Analysis | mutation_overlap, frequency | Pairwise mutation overlap and bootstrap frequency estimation |\n\n### Task Inventory\n\n#### Task: `individuals`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/individuals.py`\n- **Purpose**: Parse a VCF file chunk (defined by start/stop line numbers) and extract per-individual mutation calls, applying allele frequency filters.\n- **Parallelism**: Configurable fan-out — `ind_jobs` chunks per chromosome (default 1, up to 250). Each chunk processes a disjoint line range of the VCF.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - VCF file for chromosome `c` (`ALL.chr{c}.250000.vcf`)\n  - `columns.txt` (individual ID list, 2504 entries)\n  - Command-line args: chromosome number, start line, stop line, total lines\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` — compressed archive of per-individual files within a directory `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}/`; each file `chr{c}.{individual_id}` contains tab-delimited: POS, ID, REF, ALT, AF\n- **Filter logic**: Retains mutations where (AF >= 0.5 AND first allele = 0) OR (AF < 0.5 AND first allele = 1) — identifies individuals with unexpected alleles.\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound (reads large VCF, writes many small per-individual files)\n\n#### Task: `individuals_merge`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/individuals_merge.py`\n- **Purpose**: Merge all parallel `individuals` output chunks for one chromosome into a single archive.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per chromosome (serial fan-in).\n- **Inputs**:\n  - All `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` chunks for chromosome `c` (variable count matching `ind_jobs`)\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n.tar.gz` — merged archive containing unified per-individual files for chromosome `c`\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound (reads and re-writes compressed archives)\n\n#### Task: `sifting`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/sifting.py`\n- **Purpose**: Filter the SIFT functional annotation VCF for chromosome `c`, extracting records labeled \"deleterious\" or \"tolerated\" that have rs-number identifiers, and writing a structured text summary.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per chromosome (independent of individuals stage).\n- **Inputs**:\n  - SIFT annotation VCF: `ALL.chr{c}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf`\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` — tab-delimited: line_num, rs_id, ENSG_id, SIFT_prediction, phenotype_score\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound (sequential line-by-line read of large VCF, filtered write)\n\n#### Task: `mutation_overlap`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/mutation_overlap.py`\n- **Purpose**: For a given (chromosome, population) pair, compute pairwise mutation overlaps among individuals using SIFT-filtered variants. Generates overlap matrices (total, half, random), gene-pair frequency tables, and visualization plots.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per (chromosome × population) — up to 70 jobs (10 chr × 7 populations) concurrently.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n.tar.gz` (merged individuals archive)\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` (SIFT scores)\n  - Population file (e.g., `data/populations/AFR`) listing individual IDs for the population\n  - `columns.txt` (reference individual list)\n  - Args: `-c {chromosome}`, `-pop {population}`\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}-{pop}.tar.gz` containing:\n    - `output_no_sift/total_mutations_individual{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/total_individual_pairs_overlap_chr{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/individual_half_pairs_overlap_chr{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/100_individual_overlap_chr{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/random_mutations_individual{c}_s*_run_0.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/gene_pairs_count_chr{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/mutation_index_array{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/map_variations{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `plots_no_sift/total_distribution_c{c}_s*.png`\n    - `plots_no_sift/half_distribution_c{c}_s*.png`\n    - `plots_no_sift/100_distribution_c{c}_s*.png`\n    - `plots_no_sift/colormap_distribution_c{c}_s*.png`\n- **io_dominance**: balanced (CPU-intensive overlap computation + I/O for reading and writing archives)\n\n#### Task: `frequency`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/frequency.py`\n- **Purpose**: Bootstrap mutation frequency estimation for a (chromosome, population) pair. Runs 1000 iterations of randomly sampling 52 individuals and counting mutation frequencies.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per (chromosome × population) — up to 70 jobs concurrently, independent of `mutation_overlap`.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - Same as `mutation_overlap`: `chr{c}n.tar.gz`, `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt`, population file, `columns.txt`\n  - Args: `-c {chromosome}`, `-pop {population}`\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz` containing per-run files (1000 runs):\n    - `output_no_sift/Histogram_mutation_overlap_chr{c}_s*_{run_N}.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/Mutation_overlap_chr{c}_s*_{run_N}.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/random_indiv_chr{c}_s*_{run_N}.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/mutation_index_array{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/map_variations{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `plots_no_sift/Frequency_mutations{c}_s*{run_N}.png` (1000 plots)\n- **io_dominance**: compute_bound (1000 bootstrap iterations, random sampling; heavy CPU for frequency counting)\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Data Object Registry\n\n| Data ID | Name / Pattern | Format | Category | Persistence | Description |\n|---------|----------------|--------|----------|-------------|-------------|\n| data:vcf_chr | `ALL.chr{c}.250000.vcf` | VCF (tab-delimited text) | input | persistent | Phase 3 genotype calls for 2504 individuals, 250k variants, one per chromosome |\n| data:sift_vcf_chr | `ALL.chr{c}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf` | VCF (text) | input | persistent | VEP functional annotation VCF with SIFT scores per variant |\n| data:columns_txt | `columns.txt` | plain text | input | persistent | Ordered list of 2504 individual IDs (column headers for genotype matrix) |\n| data:population_file | `data/populations/{POP}` | plain text (whitespace-separated IDs) | input | persistent | One file per population (AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) listing individual IDs |\n| data:individuals_chunk | `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` | tar.gz of per-individual text files | intermediate | transient | Per-individual mutation files for a line range of one chromosome; one per parallel individuals job |\n| data:individuals_merged | `chr{c}n.tar.gz` | tar.gz of per-individual text files | intermediate | stage_scoped | Merged per-individual mutation files for an entire chromosome; consumed by mutation_overlap and frequency |\n| data:sift_scores | `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` | tab-delimited text | intermediate | stage_scoped | Filtered SIFT functional annotation table per chromosome; consumed by mutation_overlap and frequency |\n| data:overlap_results | `chr{c}-{pop}.tar.gz` | tar.gz (txt + png) | output | persistent | Pairwise mutation overlap matrices, gene-pair tables, and histograms/heatmaps for one (chr, pop) pair |\n| data:frequency_results | `chr{c}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz` | tar.gz (txt + png) | output | persistent | Bootstrap frequency histograms and per-run mutation tables for one (chr, pop) pair (1000 runs) |\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Producer-Consumer Edges\n\n| Edge | Producer Task | Consumer Task | Data Object(s) | Edge Pattern | Coupling | Rationale |\n|------|--------------|---------------|----------------|-------------|----------|-----------|\n| edge:individuals->merge | individuals | individuals_merge | `data:individuals_chunk` | n_to_1 | loose | Multiple parallel individuals jobs (n chunks) produce separate tar.gz files; merge waits for all before combining |\n| edge:merge->overlap | individuals_merge | mutation_overlap | `data:individuals_merged` | 1_to_n | loose | Single merged archive per chromosome fans out to all 7 population overlap jobs for that chromosome |\n| edge:merge->frequency | individuals_merge | frequency | `data:individuals_merged` | 1_to_n | loose | Same merged archive also fans out to all 7 population frequency jobs — data reuse across two consumer tasks |\n| edge:sifting->overlap | sifting | mutation_overlap | `data:sift_scores` | 1_to_n | loose | Single SIFT scores file per chromosome fans out to all 7 population overlap jobs |\n| edge:sifting->frequency | sifting | frequency | `data:sift_scores` | 1_to_n | loose | Same SIFT scores file also consumed by all 7 frequency jobs per chromosome — data reuse |\n\n### Communication Pattern\n\nAll inter-task communication uses **shared files** (tar.gz archives and text files on a shared/distributed filesystem). No in-memory or streaming data transfer is observed in the code. Data staging is file-based as orchestrated by Pegasus.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Workflow-Level Pattern\n\n### DAG Structure\n\n```\n[VCF input]        [SIFT annotation VCF]      [columns.txt]   [population files]\n     |                       |                      |                  |\n     v                       v                      |                  |\n individuals            sifting ─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n (n parallel                 |                      |                         |\n  chunks/chr)                |                      |                         |\n     |                       |                      |                         |\n     └──── (n_to_1) ─────────|──────────────────────┤                         |\n                             |                      |                         |\n                       individuals_merge            |                         |\n                             |                      |                         |\n                 ┌───────────┴───────────┐          |                         |\n                 | (1_to_n per chr×pop)  |          |                         |\n                 v                       v          |                         |\n           mutation_overlap           frequency ◄───┘─────────────────────────┘\n           (chr×pop parallel)         (chr×pop parallel)\n                 |                       |\n                 v                       v\n          overlap_results         frequency_results\n```\n\n### Pattern Classification\n\n**Primary pattern**: `scatter_gather` + `pipeline` (hybrid)\n\n- **Scatter-gather**: The `individuals` task scatters per-chromosome VCF into `n` parallel chunks; `individuals_merge` gathers them back into one archive per chromosome.\n- **Pipeline**: A linear chain of stages runs: extract → merge → analyze. The analysis stage (`mutation_overlap`, `frequency`) cannot start until both `individuals_merge` and `sifting` complete for that chromosome.\n- **Parallel fan-out at analysis**: `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` both run in an embarrassingly parallel grid (10 chromosomes × 7 populations = 70 jobs each). These two tasks are independent of each other (no data dependency between them) and can run concurrently.\n- **Broadcast fan-out**: `data:individuals_merged` and `data:sift_scores` are each read by multiple downstream jobs (data reuse, 1-to-n edges).\n\n**No iteration or feedback loops** are present. The DAG is a strict forward-only acyclic graph.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: I/O Behavioral Hints\n\n| Concern | Location | Evidence | Notes |\n|---------|----------|----------|-------|\n| `small_file_overhead` | `individuals.py` output | Each individuals job writes one file per individual inside a tar.gz archive. With 2504 individuals and up to 250 parallel chunks, this produces hundreds of thousands of small per-individual files before compression. The tar.gz wrapper mitigates this for staging but the in-memory assembly before compression is a concern. | Compression at the task boundary reduces staging overhead but internal file count within each tar.gz is very high. |\n| `data_reuse` | `individuals_merge` → `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` | `chr{c}n.tar.gz` (data:individuals_merged) is read by both `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` for the same chromosome. Similarly, `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` is read by both tasks per chromosome. | Each consumer independently extracts and reads the same archive; no shared cache. Up to 7 × 2 = 14 redundant reads of each merged archive per chromosome. |\n| `small_file_overhead` | `frequency.py` output | 1000 bootstrap runs each write separate output files (histogram txt, mutation overlap txt, random individual list, per-run PNG). With 70 jobs (10 chr × 7 pop), total output can reach 70,000+ small files, then compressed into tar.gz per job. | The per-run PNG generation (1000 plots per job) is particularly file-intensive. |\n| `unnecessary_serialization` | `mutation_overlap.py`, `frequency.py` | Both tasks independently extract and re-parse the same `chr{c}n.tar.gz` and SIFT text file. There is no shared in-memory representation between these co-located tasks. | [ASSUMPTION] If scheduled on the same node, these tasks could share parsed data structures but the implementation does not support this. |\n| `partial_access` | `individuals.py` | Each parallel individuals job reads only a specific line range (start–stop) of the VCF file, requiring a full sequential scan up to the start line (no random access / byte-offset indexing is visible in code). | Depending on the file system, this may cause repeated head-of-file reads across parallel jobs on the same VCF. |\n| `metadata_overhead` | `sifting.py` | The SIFT annotation VCF is a large file (complete annotation for all variants), but sifting filters to only \"deleterious\" or \"tolerated\" variants with rs-numbers. The final output (`sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt`) is much smaller. | Low concern — one job per chromosome, sequential scan. |\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Summary and Cross-Reference Validation\n\n### Workflow Summary\n\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Workflow name | 1000genome |\n| Orchestrator | Pegasus (DAX/YAML), generated by `daxgen.py` |\n| Number of stages | 4 |\n| Number of task types | 5 |\n| Data granularity | Per-chromosome (10 chromosomes) × per-population (7 populations) |\n| Maximum concurrency | Up to 140+ simultaneous jobs at analysis stage (70 overlap + 70 frequency) |\n| Primary pattern | scatter_gather + pipeline (hybrid) |\n| Data exchange mechanism | Shared filesystem (tar.gz archives and text files) |\n| Output volume | 70 overlap result archives + 70 frequency archives (each containing 1000+ files) |\n\n### Cross-Reference Validation\n\n- All task inputs reference data objects defined in the data object registry. ✓\n- All producer-consumer edges reference valid task IDs and data object IDs. ✓\n- No deployment, scheduler, or hardware-specific details included in task descriptions. ✓\n- Sifting stage is independent of individuals stage and can run concurrently. ✓ (Confirmed: no data dependency between them.)\n- `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` are independent of each other (no data flows between them). ✓\n- All population files (7) and chromosomes (10) confirmed from `data.csv` and `data/populations/`. ✓\n\n### Unresolved / Unknown Items\n\n- **Per-job VCF line range access pattern**: Whether the filesystem supports efficient random access at line boundaries is `unknown` from code alone; `individuals.py` appears to do sequential reads.\n- **Analysis stage input for bash variant**: `daxgen.py` supports a `use_bash` flag implying bash-script equivalents of Python tasks may exist; their I/O contract is assumed equivalent. [ASSUMPTION]\n- **Exact output file naming suffix `s*`**: The suffix in output filenames (e.g., `total_mutations_individual{c}_s...txt`) depends on runtime arguments not fully traceable from static analysis alone. The pattern is present in the code but the exact suffix value is `unknown`.\n"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DYWpLmUfPfg5opVjW9L1Yx","tool_input":{"file_path":"/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial3.md","content":"# Workflow Knowledge Report: 1000 Genomes\n\n**Workflow**: 1000genome\n**Agent**: claude\n**Date**: 2026-03-04\n**Source**: Static analysis of `/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow`\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Repository Survey\n\n### Entry Points and Structure\n\n```\n1000genome-workflow/\n├── daxgen.py              # Main workflow generator (Pegasus DAX/YAML)\n├── data.csv               # Input manifest: 10 chromosomes × VCF + SIFT annotation paths\n├── prepare_input.sh       # Downloads/unzips raw input data (not part of workflow logic)\n├── env.sh                 # Environment setup for Decaf in-memory execution (deployment only)\n├── ares_1kgenome_parallel.sbatch  # HPC batch submission script\n├── bin/\n│   ├── individuals.py     # Task: parse VCF and extract per-individual mutations\n│   ├── individuals_merge.py  # Task: merge parallel individual chunks\n│   ├── sifting.py         # Task: extract SIFT functional annotation scores\n│   ├── mutation_overlap.py   # Task: pairwise overlap analysis + visualization\n│   └── frequency.py       # Task: bootstrap mutation frequency estimation\n├── data/\n│   ├── 20130502/          # Input VCF and SIFT annotation files\n│   │   ├── chr1n/         # Sample individual-level files\n│   │   ├── sifting/       # SIFT annotation VCFs\n│   │   └── columns.txt    # 2504 individual IDs (column headers)\n│   └── populations/       # Population membership files: AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS\n└── analysis/              # Post-hoc analysis scripts (not part of core workflow)\n```\n\n**Orchestration**: `daxgen.py` generates a Pegasus workflow DAX (YAML format) that defines all tasks, file dependencies, and execution sites. The workflow engine drives task scheduling.\n\n**Key Configuration File**: `data.csv` lists one row per chromosome: `filename, num_rows, sift_file`.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Stages and Tasks\n\n### Stage Grouping\n\n| Stage ID | Stage Name | Tasks | Description |\n|----------|-----------|-------|-------------|\n| stage:individuals | Individuals Extraction | individuals | Parse VCF files to extract per-individual SNP mutations |\n| stage:merge | Individuals Merge | individuals_merge | Merge parallel per-chromosome chunks |\n| stage:sifting | SIFT Annotation | sifting | Extract functional effect predictions from annotation VCF |\n| stage:analysis | Overlap Analysis | mutation_overlap, frequency | Pairwise mutation overlap and bootstrap frequency estimation |\n\n### Task Inventory\n\n#### Task: `individuals`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/individuals.py`\n- **Purpose**: Parse a VCF file chunk (defined by start/stop line numbers) and extract per-individual mutation calls, applying allele frequency filters.\n- **Parallelism**: Configurable fan-out — `ind_jobs` chunks per chromosome (default 1, up to 250). Each chunk processes a disjoint line range of the VCF.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - VCF file for chromosome `c` (`ALL.chr{c}.250000.vcf`)\n  - `columns.txt` (individual ID list, 2504 entries)\n  - Command-line args: chromosome number, start line, stop line, total lines\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` — compressed archive of per-individual files within a directory `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}/`; each file `chr{c}.{individual_id}` contains tab-delimited: POS, ID, REF, ALT, AF\n- **Filter logic**: Retains mutations where (AF >= 0.5 AND first allele = 0) OR (AF < 0.5 AND first allele = 1) — identifies individuals carrying unexpected alleles.\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound (reads large VCF, writes many small per-individual files)\n\n#### Task: `individuals_merge`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/individuals_merge.py`\n- **Purpose**: Merge all parallel `individuals` output chunks for one chromosome into a single archive.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per chromosome (serial fan-in).\n- **Inputs**:\n  - All `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` chunks for chromosome `c` (variable count matching `ind_jobs`)\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n.tar.gz` — merged archive containing unified per-individual files for chromosome `c`\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound (reads and re-writes compressed archives)\n\n#### Task: `sifting`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/sifting.py`\n- **Purpose**: Filter the SIFT functional annotation VCF for chromosome `c`, extracting records labeled \"deleterious\" or \"tolerated\" that have rs-number identifiers, and writing a structured text summary.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per chromosome (independent of individuals stage).\n- **Inputs**:\n  - SIFT annotation VCF: `ALL.chr{c}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf`\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` — tab-delimited: line_num, rs_id, ENSG_id, SIFT_prediction, phenotype_score\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound (sequential line-by-line read of large VCF, filtered write)\n\n#### Task: `mutation_overlap`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/mutation_overlap.py`\n- **Purpose**: For a given (chromosome, population) pair, compute pairwise mutation overlaps among individuals using SIFT-filtered variants. Generates overlap matrices (total, half, random), gene-pair frequency tables, and visualization plots.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per (chromosome × population) — up to 70 jobs (10 chr × 7 populations) concurrently.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n.tar.gz` (merged individuals archive)\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` (SIFT scores)\n  - Population file (e.g., `data/populations/AFR`) listing individual IDs for the population\n  - `columns.txt` (reference individual list)\n  - Args: `-c {chromosome}`, `-pop {population}`\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}-{pop}.tar.gz` containing:\n    - `output_no_sift/total_mutations_individual{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/total_individual_pairs_overlap_chr{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/individual_half_pairs_overlap_chr{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/100_individual_overlap_chr{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/random_mutations_individual{c}_s*_run_0.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/gene_pairs_count_chr{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/mutation_index_array{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/map_variations{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `plots_no_sift/total_distribution_c{c}_s*.png`\n    - `plots_no_sift/half_distribution_c{c}_s*.png`\n    - `plots_no_sift/100_distribution_c{c}_s*.png`\n    - `plots_no_sift/colormap_distribution_c{c}_s*.png`\n- **io_dominance**: balanced (CPU-intensive overlap computation + I/O for reading and writing archives)\n\n#### Task: `frequency`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/frequency.py`\n- **Purpose**: Bootstrap mutation frequency estimation for a (chromosome, population) pair. Runs 1000 iterations of randomly sampling 52 individuals and counting mutation frequencies.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per (chromosome × population) — up to 70 jobs concurrently, independent of `mutation_overlap`.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - Same as `mutation_overlap`: `chr{c}n.tar.gz`, `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt`, population file, `columns.txt`\n  - Args: `-c {chromosome}`, `-pop {population}`\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz` containing per-run files (1000 runs):\n    - `output_no_sift/Histogram_mutation_overlap_chr{c}_s*_{run_N}.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/Mutation_overlap_chr{c}_s*_{run_N}.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/random_indiv_chr{c}_s*_{run_N}.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/mutation_index_array{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `output_no_sift/map_variations{c}_s*.txt`\n    - `plots_no_sift/Frequency_mutations{c}_s*{run_N}.png` (1000 plots per job)\n- **io_dominance**: compute_bound (1000 bootstrap iterations; heavy CPU for frequency counting)\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Data Object Registry\n\n| Data ID | Name / Pattern | Format | Category | Persistence | Description |\n|---------|----------------|--------|----------|-------------|-------------|\n| data:vcf_chr | `ALL.chr{c}.250000.vcf` | VCF (tab-delimited text) | input | persistent | Phase 3 genotype calls for 2504 individuals, 250k variants, one per chromosome |\n| data:sift_vcf_chr | `ALL.chr{c}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf` | VCF (text) | input | persistent | VEP functional annotation VCF with SIFT scores per variant |\n| data:columns_txt | `columns.txt` | plain text | input | persistent | Ordered list of 2504 individual IDs (column headers for genotype matrix) |\n| data:population_file | `data/populations/{POP}` | plain text (whitespace-separated IDs) | input | persistent | One file per population (AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) listing individual IDs |\n| data:individuals_chunk | `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` | tar.gz of per-individual text files | intermediate | transient | Per-individual mutation files for a line range of one chromosome; one per parallel individuals job |\n| data:individuals_merged | `chr{c}n.tar.gz` | tar.gz of per-individual text files | intermediate | stage_scoped | Merged per-individual mutation files for an entire chromosome; consumed by mutation_overlap and frequency |\n| data:sift_scores | `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` | tab-delimited text | intermediate | stage_scoped | Filtered SIFT functional annotation table per chromosome; consumed by mutation_overlap and frequency |\n| data:overlap_results | `chr{c}-{pop}.tar.gz` | tar.gz (txt + png) | output | persistent | Pairwise mutation overlap matrices, gene-pair tables, and histograms/heatmaps for one (chr, pop) pair |\n| data:frequency_results | `chr{c}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz` | tar.gz (txt + png) | output | persistent | Bootstrap frequency histograms and per-run mutation tables for one (chr, pop) pair (1000 runs) |\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Producer-Consumer Edges\n\n| Edge | Producer Task | Consumer Task | Data Object(s) | Edge Pattern | Coupling | Rationale |\n|------|--------------|---------------|----------------|-------------|----------|-----------|\n| edge:individuals->merge | individuals | individuals_merge | `data:individuals_chunk` | n_to_1 | loose | Multiple parallel individuals jobs (n chunks) produce separate tar.gz files; merge waits for all before combining |\n| edge:merge->overlap | individuals_merge | mutation_overlap | `data:individuals_merged` | 1_to_n | loose | Single merged archive per chromosome fans out to all 7 population overlap jobs for that chromosome |\n| edge:merge->frequency | individuals_merge | frequency | `data:individuals_merged` | 1_to_n | loose | Same merged archive also fans out to all 7 population frequency jobs — data reuse across two consumer tasks |\n| edge:sifting->overlap | sifting | mutation_overlap | `data:sift_scores` | 1_to_n | loose | Single SIFT scores file per chromosome fans out to all 7 population overlap jobs |\n| edge:sifting->frequency | sifting | frequency | `data:sift_scores` | 1_to_n | loose | Same SIFT scores file also consumed by all 7 frequency jobs per chromosome — data reuse |\n\n### Communication Pattern\n\nAll inter-task communication uses **shared files** (tar.gz archives and text files on a shared/distributed filesystem). No in-memory or streaming data transfer is observed in the code. Data staging is file-based as orchestrated by Pegasus.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Workflow-Level Pattern\n\n### DAG Structure\n\n```\n[VCF input]        [SIFT annotation VCF]    [columns.txt]   [population files]\n     |                       |                    |                  |\n     v                       v                    |                  |\n individuals            sifting                   |                  |\n (n parallel            (per chr,                 |                  |\n  chunks/chr)            independent)             |                  |\n     |                       |                    |                  |\n     └──── (n_to_1) ─────────|────────────────────┤                  |\n                             |                    |                  |\n                       individuals_merge          |                  |\n                             |                    |                  |\n              ┌──────────────┴──────────┐         |                  |\n              | (1_to_n per chr×pop)    |         |                  |\n              v                         v         |                  |\n        mutation_overlap            frequency ◄───┴──────────────────┘\n        (chr×pop parallel)          (chr×pop parallel)\n              |                         |\n              v                         v\n       overlap_results           frequency_results\n```\n\n### Pattern Classification\n\n**Primary pattern**: `scatter_gather` + `pipeline` (hybrid)\n\n- **Scatter-gather**: The `individuals` task scatters per-chromosome VCF into `n` parallel chunks; `individuals_merge` gathers them back into one archive per chromosome.\n- **Pipeline**: A linear chain of stages runs: extract → merge → analyze. The analysis stage cannot start until both `individuals_merge` and `sifting` complete for that chromosome.\n- **Parallel fan-out at analysis**: `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` both run in an embarrassingly parallel grid (10 chromosomes × 7 populations = 70 jobs each). These two tasks are independent of each other and can run concurrently.\n- **Broadcast fan-out**: `data:individuals_merged` and `data:sift_scores` are each read by multiple downstream jobs (data reuse, 1-to-n edges).\n\n**No iteration or feedback loops** are present. The DAG is a strict forward-only acyclic graph.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: I/O Behavioral Hints\n\n| Concern | Location | Evidence | Notes |\n|---------|----------|----------|-------|\n| `small_file_overhead` | `individuals.py` output | Each individuals job writes one file per individual inside a tar.gz archive. With 2504 individuals and up to 250 parallel chunks, this produces hundreds of thousands of small per-individual files before compression. The tar.gz wrapper mitigates staging overhead but internal file count within each archive is very high. | Compression at task boundary reduces staging cost but in-memory assembly of many small files is a concern. |\n| `data_reuse` | `individuals_merge` → `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` | `chr{c}n.tar.gz` (data:individuals_merged) is read by both `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` for the same chromosome. Similarly, `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` is read by both tasks per chromosome. Each consumer independently extracts and re-reads the same archive with no shared cache. | Up to 7 × 2 = 14 redundant reads of each merged archive and SIFT file per chromosome. |\n| `small_file_overhead` | `frequency.py` output | 1000 bootstrap runs each write separate output files (histogram txt, mutation overlap txt, random individual list, per-run PNG). With 70 jobs (10 chr × 7 pop), total output can reach 70,000+ small files compressed into tar.gz per job. The per-run PNG generation (1000 plots per job) is particularly file-intensive. | Output archive wrapping reduces staging cost but internal file count is very high. |\n| `unnecessary_serialization` | `mutation_overlap.py`, `frequency.py` | Both tasks independently extract and re-parse the same `chr{c}n.tar.gz` and SIFT text file. There is no shared in-memory representation between these co-located tasks. | [ASSUMPTION] If scheduled on the same node, these tasks could share parsed data structures but the current implementation does not support this. |\n| `partial_access` | `individuals.py` | Each parallel individuals job reads only a specific line range (start–stop) of the VCF file. The code iterates lines sequentially without byte-offset indexing, likely requiring a full sequential scan from the file start to reach the start line. | Depending on the filesystem, this may cause repeated head-of-file reads across parallel jobs on the same VCF. |\n| `metadata_overhead` | `sifting.py` | The SIFT annotation VCF is a large file containing annotations for all variants, but sifting filters to only \"deleterious\" or \"tolerated\" variants with rs-numbers. The final output is much smaller than the input. | Low concern — one job per chromosome, single sequential scan. |\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Summary and Cross-Reference Validation\n\n### Workflow Summary\n\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Workflow name | 1000genome |\n| Orchestrator | Pegasus (DAX/YAML), generated by `daxgen.py` |\n| Number of stages | 4 |\n| Number of task types | 5 |\n| Data granularity | Per-chromosome (10 chromosomes) × per-population (7 populations) |\n| Maximum concurrency | Up to 140+ simultaneous jobs at analysis stage (70 overlap + 70 frequency) |\n| Primary pattern | scatter_gather + pipeline (hybrid) |\n| Data exchange mechanism | Shared filesystem (tar.gz archives and text files) |\n| Output volume | 70 overlap result archives + 70 frequency archives (each containing 1000+ files internally) |\n\n### Cross-Reference Validation\n\n- All task inputs reference data objects defined in the data object registry. ✓\n- All producer-consumer edges reference valid task IDs and data object IDs. ✓\n- No deployment, scheduler, or hardware-specific details included in task descriptions. ✓\n- Sifting stage is independent of individuals stage and can run concurrently — no data dependency between them. ✓\n- `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` are independent of each other — no data flows between them. ✓\n- All 7 population files and 10 chromosomes confirmed from `data.csv` and `data/populations/`. ✓\n\n### Unresolved / Unknown Items\n\n- **Per-job VCF line range access pattern**: Whether the filesystem supports efficient random access at line boundaries is `unknown` from code alone; `individuals.py` appears to do sequential reads from the beginning.\n- **Bash script equivalents**: `daxgen.py` supports a `use_bash` flag implying bash-script equivalents of Python tasks; their exact I/O contract is assumed equivalent to the Python scripts. [ASSUMPTION]\n- **Exact output filename suffix**: The suffix in output filenames (e.g., `total_mutations_individual{c}_s*.txt`) depends on runtime argument values not fully determinable from static analysis. [ASSUMPTION: pattern reflects runtime chromosome/population identifiers]\n"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_016HC2nVmt5XzaSuqQJuBwzo","tool_input":{"command":"cat > /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial3.md << 'MDEOF'\n# Workflow Knowledge Report: 1000 Genomes\n\n**Workflow**: 1000genome\n**Agent**: claude\n**Date**: 2026-03-04\n**Source**: Static analysis of `/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow`\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Repository Survey\n\n### Entry Points and Structure\n\n```\n1000genome-workflow/\n├── daxgen.py              # Main workflow generator (Pegasus DAX/YAML)\n├── data.csv               # Input manifest: 10 chromosomes × VCF + SIFT annotation paths\n├── prepare_input.sh       # Downloads/unzips raw input data (not part of workflow logic)\n├── env.sh                 # Environment setup for Decaf (deployment only)\n├── ares_1kgenome_parallel.sbatch  # HPC batch submission script\n├── bin/\n│   ├── individuals.py     # Task: parse VCF and extract per-individual mutations\n│   ├── individuals_merge.py  # Task: merge parallel individual chunks\n│   ├── sifting.py         # Task: extract SIFT functional annotation scores\n│   ├── mutation_overlap.py   # Task: pairwise overlap analysis + visualization\n│   └── frequency.py       # Task: bootstrap mutation frequency estimation\n├── data/\n│   ├── 20130502/          # Input VCF and SIFT annotation files\n│   │   ├── chr1n/         # Sample individual-level files\n│   │   ├── sifting/       # SIFT annotation VCFs\n│   │   └── columns.txt    # 2504 individual IDs (column headers)\n│   └── populations/       # Population membership files: AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS\n└── analysis/              # Post-hoc analysis scripts (not part of core workflow)\n```\n\n**Orchestration**: `daxgen.py` generates a Pegasus workflow DAX (YAML format) defining all tasks, file dependencies, and execution sites.\n\n**Key Configuration File**: `data.csv` — one row per chromosome: `filename, num_rows, sift_file` (10 entries for chr1–chr10).\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Stages and Tasks\n\n### Stage Grouping\n\n| Stage ID | Stage Name | Tasks | Description |\n|----------|-----------|-------|-------------|\n| stage:individuals | Individuals Extraction | individuals | Parse VCF files to extract per-individual SNP mutations |\n| stage:merge | Individuals Merge | individuals_merge | Merge parallel per-chromosome chunks |\n| stage:sifting | SIFT Annotation | sifting | Extract functional effect predictions from annotation VCF |\n| stage:analysis | Overlap Analysis | mutation_overlap, frequency | Pairwise mutation overlap and bootstrap frequency estimation |\n\n### Task Details\n\n#### Task: `individuals`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/individuals.py`\n- **Purpose**: Parse a VCF file chunk (defined by start/stop line numbers) and extract per-individual mutation calls with allele frequency filtering.\n- **Parallelism**: Configurable fan-out — `ind_jobs` chunks per chromosome (default 1, up to 250). Each chunk processes a disjoint line range.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - `ALL.chr{c}.250000.vcf` — VCF for chromosome c\n  - `columns.txt` — ordered individual ID list (2504 entries)\n  - Args: chromosome number, start line, stop line, total lines\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` — archive of per-individual files; each file `chr{c}.{individual_id}` with tab-delimited: POS, ID, REF, ALT, AF\n- **Filter logic**: Retains mutations where (AF >= 0.5 AND first allele = 0) OR (AF < 0.5 AND first allele = 1).\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound\n\n#### Task: `individuals_merge`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/individuals_merge.py`\n- **Purpose**: Merge all parallel `individuals` output chunks for one chromosome into a single archive.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per chromosome (fan-in).\n- **Inputs**: All `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` chunks for chromosome c\n- **Outputs**: `chr{c}n.tar.gz` — merged per-individual files for chromosome c\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound\n\n#### Task: `sifting`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/sifting.py`\n- **Purpose**: Filter SIFT functional annotation VCF, extracting \"deleterious\"/\"tolerated\" variants with rs-number identifiers.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per chromosome, independent of individuals stage.\n- **Inputs**: `ALL.chr{c}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf`\n- **Outputs**: `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` — tab-delimited: line_num, rs_id, ENSG_id, SIFT_prediction, phenotype_score\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound\n\n#### Task: `mutation_overlap`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/mutation_overlap.py`\n- **Purpose**: For a (chromosome, population) pair, compute pairwise mutation overlaps among individuals using SIFT-filtered variants. Produces overlap matrices, gene-pair frequency tables, and visualization plots.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per (chromosome × population) — up to 70 jobs (10 chr × 7 populations) concurrently.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n.tar.gz` (merged individuals archive)\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` (SIFT scores)\n  - `data/populations/{POP}` (population individual ID list)\n  - `columns.txt`\n  - Args: `-c {chromosome}`, `-pop {population}`\n- **Outputs**: `chr{c}-{pop}.tar.gz` containing:\n  - `output_no_sift/`: total_mutations, total_pairs_overlap, half_pairs_overlap, 100_overlap, random_mutations, gene_pairs_count, mutation_index_array, map_variations (all .txt)\n  - `plots_no_sift/`: total_distribution, half_distribution, 100_distribution, colormap_distribution (.png)\n- **io_dominance**: balanced\n\n#### Task: `frequency`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/frequency.py`\n- **Purpose**: Bootstrap mutation frequency estimation for a (chromosome, population) pair — 1000 iterations of randomly sampling 52 individuals and counting mutation frequencies.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per (chromosome × population) — up to 70 jobs concurrently, independent of `mutation_overlap`.\n- **Inputs**: Same as `mutation_overlap` (chr{c}n.tar.gz, sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt, population file, columns.txt)\n- **Outputs**: `chr{c}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz` containing per-run files (1000 runs each):\n  - `output_no_sift/`: Histogram_mutation_overlap, Mutation_overlap, random_indiv, mutation_index_array, map_variations\n  - `plots_no_sift/`: Frequency_mutations per run (1000 .png files per job)\n- **io_dominance**: compute_bound\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Data Object Registry\n\n| Data ID | Name / Pattern | Format | Category | Persistence | Description |\n|---------|----------------|--------|----------|-------------|-------------|\n| data:vcf_chr | `ALL.chr{c}.250000.vcf` | VCF (tab-delimited) | input | persistent | Phase 3 genotype calls, 2504 individuals, 250k variants, one per chromosome |\n| data:sift_vcf_chr | `ALL.chr{c}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf` | VCF (text) | input | persistent | VEP functional annotation VCF with SIFT scores per variant |\n| data:columns_txt | `columns.txt` | plain text | input | persistent | Ordered list of 2504 individual IDs (genotype matrix column headers) |\n| data:population_file | `data/populations/{POP}` | plain text (whitespace-separated) | input | persistent | One file per population listing individual IDs (7 files: AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) |\n| data:individuals_chunk | `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` | tar.gz of per-individual text files | intermediate | transient | Per-individual mutation files for a line range of one chromosome; one per parallel individuals job |\n| data:individuals_merged | `chr{c}n.tar.gz` | tar.gz of per-individual text files | intermediate | stage_scoped | Merged per-individual mutation files for an entire chromosome; consumed by both mutation_overlap and frequency |\n| data:sift_scores | `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` | tab-delimited text | intermediate | stage_scoped | Filtered SIFT annotation table per chromosome; consumed by both mutation_overlap and frequency |\n| data:overlap_results | `chr{c}-{pop}.tar.gz` | tar.gz (txt + png) | output | persistent | Pairwise mutation overlap matrices, gene-pair tables, and plots for one (chr, pop) pair |\n| data:frequency_results | `chr{c}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz` | tar.gz (txt + png) | output | persistent | Bootstrap frequency histograms and per-run mutation tables for one (chr, pop) pair (1000 runs) |\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Producer-Consumer Edges\n\n| Edge | Producer | Consumer | Data Object(s) | Pattern | Coupling | Rationale |\n|------|----------|----------|----------------|---------|----------|-----------|\n| edge:individuals->merge | individuals | individuals_merge | data:individuals_chunk | n_to_1 | loose | n parallel chunks fan-in to single merge per chromosome |\n| edge:merge->overlap | individuals_merge | mutation_overlap | data:individuals_merged | 1_to_n | loose | Single merged archive fans out to 7 population overlap jobs per chromosome |\n| edge:merge->frequency | individuals_merge | frequency | data:individuals_merged | 1_to_n | loose | Same merged archive fans out to 7 population frequency jobs — data reuse |\n| edge:sifting->overlap | sifting | mutation_overlap | data:sift_scores | 1_to_n | loose | Single SIFT file fans out to 7 population overlap jobs per chromosome |\n| edge:sifting->frequency | sifting | frequency | data:sift_scores | 1_to_n | loose | Same SIFT file fans out to 7 population frequency jobs — data reuse |\n\n**Communication pattern**: All inter-task data exchange is via shared filesystem files (tar.gz archives and text files). No in-memory or streaming transfer observed in code.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Workflow-Level Pattern\n\n### DAG Structure\n\n```\n[VCF input]       [SIFT annotation VCF]    [columns.txt]  [population files]\n     |                     |                    |                 |\n     v                     v                    |                 |\n individuals           sifting                  |                 |\n (n parallel/chr)    (1/chr, independent)       |                 |\n     |                     |                    |                 |\n     └──── (n_to_1) ───────+────────────────────┤                 |\n                           |                    |                 |\n                    individuals_merge           |                 |\n                           |                   |                  |\n           ┌───────────────┴────────┐          |                  |\n           | (1_to_n per chr×pop)   |          |                  |\n           v                        v          |                  |\n    mutation_overlap            frequency  ◄───┴──────────────────┘\n    (chr×pop parallel)          (chr×pop parallel)\n           |                        |\n           v                        v\n    overlap_results          frequency_results\n```\n\n### Pattern Classification\n\n**Primary pattern**: `scatter_gather` + `pipeline` (hybrid)\n\n- **Scatter-gather**: `individuals` scatters a chromosome VCF into `n` parallel chunks; `individuals_merge` gathers them into one archive per chromosome.\n- **Pipeline**: Sequential stage chain — extract → merge → analyze. Analysis cannot start until `individuals_merge` AND `sifting` both complete for that chromosome.\n- **Embarrassingly parallel fan-out**: Both `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` run as independent grids (10 chr × 7 pop = 70 jobs each), with no inter-job dependencies within each task type.\n- **Broadcast fan-out**: `data:individuals_merged` and `data:sift_scores` are each read by multiple downstream consumers (1-to-n reuse).\n\nNo iteration or feedback loops. The DAG is strictly acyclic and forward-only.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: I/O Behavioral Hints\n\n| Concern | Location | Evidence |\n|---------|----------|----------|\n| `small_file_overhead` | `individuals.py` output | Each individuals job writes one file per individual inside tar.gz. With 2504 individuals × up to 250 parallel chunks, hundreds of thousands of small per-individual files are created before compression. Tar.gz mitigates staging cost but internal file count is very high. |\n| `data_reuse` | `individuals_merge` → `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` | `chr{c}n.tar.gz` is independently extracted and re-read by both `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` for the same chromosome. `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` is also read by both. Up to 14 redundant reads per merged archive per chromosome (7 pop × 2 tasks). No shared cache between consumers. |\n| `small_file_overhead` | `frequency.py` output | 1000 bootstrap runs produce separate txt/png files per run per job. With 70 jobs, up to 70,000+ files total before compression. 1000 PNG plots per job is particularly file-intensive. |\n| `unnecessary_serialization` | `mutation_overlap.py`, `frequency.py` | Both tasks independently extract and re-parse the same `chr{c}n.tar.gz` and SIFT text file. No shared in-memory representation between co-located tasks. [ASSUMPTION] Co-scheduling could allow data sharing but current implementation does not. |\n| `partial_access` | `individuals.py` | Each parallel individuals job reads only a specific line range of the VCF. Code iterates lines sequentially with no byte-offset indexing, likely requiring scanning from the file start to reach the partition start line. |\n| `metadata_overhead` | `sifting.py` | SIFT annotation VCF is large (all variants) but is filtered down to a small fraction (only \"deleterious\"/\"tolerated\" rs-number variants). Low concern — one sequential scan per chromosome. |\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Summary and Cross-Reference Validation\n\n### Workflow Summary\n\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Workflow name | 1000genome |\n| Orchestrator | Pegasus (DAX/YAML via daxgen.py) |\n| Number of stages | 4 |\n| Number of task types | 5 |\n| Data granularity | Per-chromosome (10) × per-population (7) |\n| Max concurrency | 140+ jobs at analysis stage (70 overlap + 70 frequency) |\n| Primary pattern | scatter_gather + pipeline (hybrid) |\n| Data exchange | Shared filesystem (tar.gz and text files) |\n| Final output | 70 overlap archives + 70 frequency archives |\n\n### Cross-Reference Validation\n\n- All task inputs reference data objects in the registry. ✓\n- All producer-consumer edges reference valid task and data IDs. ✓\n- No deployment/scheduler/hardware details in task descriptions. ✓\n- `sifting` and `individuals` stages have no data dependency — can run concurrently. ✓\n- `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` have no data dependency on each other — run concurrently. ✓\n- 10 chromosomes and 7 populations confirmed from `data.csv` and `data/populations/`. ✓\n\n### Unresolved / Unknown Items\n\n- **VCF line range access**: Whether sequential line scanning from file start occurs for each parallel individuals job is `unknown` at the filesystem level; code evidence suggests sequential reads.\n- **Bash script equivalents**: `daxgen.py` supports a `use_bash` flag; bash equivalents assumed to have the same I/O contract as Python scripts. [ASSUMPTION]\n- **Output filename suffix pattern** (e.g., `_s*`): Exact suffix values depend on runtime chromosome/population arguments — not fully determinable from static analysis. [ASSUMPTION: reflects runtime identifiers]\nMDEOF","description":"Write workflow knowledge report to output path"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_017PmnSnasrZNCJXRQVzRtVv","tool_input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\ncontent = open('/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial2.md').read()\nprint('trial2 exists, length:', len(content))\n\"","description":"Verify we can read existing file in that directory"}},{"tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01B6Sy7VJC5LbmxARHpUydXi","tool_input":{"file_path":"/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial3.md","content":"# Workflow Knowledge Report: 1000 Genomes\n\n**Workflow**: 1000genome\n**Agent**: claude\n**Date**: 2026-03-04\n**Source**: Static analysis of `/home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflows_repo/1000genome-workflow`\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Repository Survey\n\n### Entry Points and Structure\n\n```\n1000genome-workflow/\n├── daxgen.py              # Main workflow generator (Pegasus DAX/YAML)\n├── data.csv               # Input manifest: 10 chromosomes x VCF + SIFT annotation paths\n├── prepare_input.sh       # Downloads/unzips raw input data (not part of workflow logic)\n├── env.sh                 # Environment setup for Decaf (deployment only)\n├── ares_1kgenome_parallel.sbatch  # HPC batch submission script\n├── bin/\n│   ├── individuals.py        # Task: parse VCF and extract per-individual mutations\n│   ├── individuals_merge.py  # Task: merge parallel individual chunks\n│   ├── sifting.py            # Task: extract SIFT functional annotation scores\n│   ├── mutation_overlap.py   # Task: pairwise overlap analysis + visualization\n│   └── frequency.py          # Task: bootstrap mutation frequency estimation\n├── data/\n│   ├── 20130502/          # Input VCF and SIFT annotation files\n│   │   ├── chr1n/         # Sample individual-level files\n│   │   ├── sifting/       # SIFT annotation VCFs\n│   │   └── columns.txt    # 2504 individual IDs (column headers)\n│   └── populations/       # Population membership files: AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS\n└── analysis/              # Post-hoc analysis scripts (not part of core workflow)\n```\n\n**Orchestration**: `daxgen.py` generates a Pegasus workflow DAX (YAML format) defining all tasks, file dependencies, and execution sites.\n\n**Key Configuration File**: `data.csv` — one row per chromosome: `filename, num_rows, sift_file` (10 entries for chr1-chr10).\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Stages and Tasks\n\n### Stage Grouping\n\n| Stage ID | Stage Name | Tasks | Description |\n|----------|-----------|-------|-------------|\n| stage:individuals | Individuals Extraction | individuals | Parse VCF files to extract per-individual SNP mutations |\n| stage:merge | Individuals Merge | individuals_merge | Merge parallel per-chromosome chunks |\n| stage:sifting | SIFT Annotation | sifting | Extract functional effect predictions from annotation VCF |\n| stage:analysis | Overlap Analysis | mutation_overlap, frequency | Pairwise mutation overlap and bootstrap frequency estimation |\n\n### Task Details\n\n#### Task: `individuals`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/individuals.py`\n- **Purpose**: Parse a VCF file chunk (defined by start/stop line numbers) and extract per-individual mutation calls with allele frequency filtering.\n- **Parallelism**: Configurable fan-out: `ind_jobs` chunks per chromosome (default 1, up to 250). Each chunk processes a disjoint line range.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - `ALL.chr{c}.250000.vcf` (VCF for chromosome c)\n  - `columns.txt` (ordered individual ID list, 2504 entries)\n  - Args: chromosome number, start line, stop line, total lines\n- **Outputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` — archive of per-individual files; each file `chr{c}.{individual_id}` contains tab-delimited: POS, ID, REF, ALT, AF\n- **Filter logic**: Retains mutations where (AF >= 0.5 AND first allele = 0) OR (AF < 0.5 AND first allele = 1) — identifies individuals carrying unexpected alleles.\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound\n\n#### Task: `individuals_merge`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/individuals_merge.py`\n- **Purpose**: Merge all parallel `individuals` output chunks for one chromosome into a single archive.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per chromosome (fan-in).\n- **Inputs**: All `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` chunks for chromosome c\n- **Outputs**: `chr{c}n.tar.gz` — merged per-individual files for chromosome c\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound\n\n#### Task: `sifting`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/sifting.py`\n- **Purpose**: Filter SIFT functional annotation VCF, extracting \"deleterious\"/\"tolerated\" variants with rs-number identifiers.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per chromosome, independent of individuals stage.\n- **Inputs**: `ALL.chr{c}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf`\n- **Outputs**: `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` — tab-delimited: line_num, rs_id, ENSG_id, SIFT_prediction, phenotype_score\n- **io_dominance**: io_bound\n\n#### Task: `mutation_overlap`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/mutation_overlap.py`\n- **Purpose**: For a (chromosome, population) pair, compute pairwise mutation overlaps among individuals using SIFT-filtered variants. Generates overlap matrices, gene-pair frequency tables, and visualization plots.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per (chromosome x population) — up to 70 jobs (10 chr x 7 populations) concurrently.\n- **Inputs**:\n  - `chr{c}n.tar.gz` (merged individuals archive)\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` (SIFT scores)\n  - `data/populations/{POP}` (population individual ID list)\n  - `columns.txt`\n  - Args: `-c {chromosome}`, `-pop {population}`\n- **Outputs**: `chr{c}-{pop}.tar.gz` containing:\n  - `output_no_sift/`: total_mutations, total_pairs_overlap, half_pairs_overlap, 100_overlap, random_mutations, gene_pairs_count, mutation_index_array, map_variations (.txt)\n  - `plots_no_sift/`: total_distribution, half_distribution, 100_distribution, colormap_distribution (.png)\n- **io_dominance**: balanced\n\n#### Task: `frequency`\n\n- **Script**: `bin/frequency.py`\n- **Purpose**: Bootstrap mutation frequency estimation for a (chromosome, population) pair. Runs 1000 iterations of randomly sampling 52 individuals and counting mutation frequencies.\n- **Parallelism**: 1 job per (chromosome x population) — up to 70 jobs concurrently, independent of `mutation_overlap`.\n- **Inputs**: Same as `mutation_overlap` (chr{c}n.tar.gz, sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt, population file, columns.txt)\n- **Outputs**: `chr{c}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz` containing per-run files (1000 runs each):\n  - `output_no_sift/`: Histogram_mutation_overlap, Mutation_overlap, random_indiv, mutation_index_array, map_variations\n  - `plots_no_sift/`: Frequency_mutations per run (1000 .png files per job)\n- **io_dominance**: compute_bound\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Data Object Registry\n\n| Data ID | Name / Pattern | Format | Category | Persistence | Description |\n|---------|----------------|--------|----------|-------------|-------------|\n| data:vcf_chr | `ALL.chr{c}.250000.vcf` | VCF (tab-delimited) | input | persistent | Phase 3 genotype calls, 2504 individuals, 250k variants, one per chromosome |\n| data:sift_vcf_chr | `ALL.chr{c}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf` | VCF (text) | input | persistent | VEP functional annotation VCF with SIFT scores per variant |\n| data:columns_txt | `columns.txt` | plain text | input | persistent | Ordered list of 2504 individual IDs (genotype matrix column headers) |\n| data:population_file | `data/populations/{POP}` | plain text | input | persistent | One file per population listing individual IDs (7 files: AFR, ALL, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) |\n| data:individuals_chunk | `chr{c}n-{start}-{stop}.tar.gz` | tar.gz of per-individual text files | intermediate | transient | Per-individual mutation files for one line range of one chromosome; one per parallel individuals job |\n| data:individuals_merged | `chr{c}n.tar.gz` | tar.gz of per-individual text files | intermediate | stage_scoped | Merged per-individual mutation files for an entire chromosome; consumed by both mutation_overlap and frequency |\n| data:sift_scores | `sifted.SIFT.chr{c}.txt` | tab-delimited text | intermediate | stage_scoped | Filtered SIFT annotation table per chromosome; consumed by both mutation_overlap and frequency |\n| data:overlap_results | `chr{c}-{pop}.tar.gz` | tar.gz (txt + png) | output | persistent | Pairwise mutation overlap matrices, gene-pair tables, and plots for one (chr, pop) pair |\n| data:frequency_results | `chr{c}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz` | tar.gz (txt + png) | output | persistent | Bootstrap frequency histograms and per-run mutation tables for one (chr, pop) pair (1000 runs) |\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Producer-Consumer Edges\n\n| Edge | Producer | Consumer | Data Object(s) | Pattern | Coupling | Rationale |\n|------|----------|----------|----------------|---------|----------|-----------|\n| edge:individuals->merge | individuals | individuals_merge | data:individuals_chunk | n_to_1 | loose | n parallel chunks fan-in to single merge per chromosome |\n| edge:merge->overlap | individuals_merge | mutation_overlap | data:individuals_merged | 1_to_n | loose | Single merged archive fans out to 7 population overlap jobs per chromosome |\n| edge:merge->frequency | individuals_merge | frequency | data:individuals_merged | 1_to_n | loose | Same merged archive fans out to 7 population frequency jobs — data reuse |\n| edge:sifting->overlap | sifting | mutation_overlap | data:sift_scores | 1_to_n | loose | Single SIFT file fans out to 7 population overlap jobs per chromosome |\n| edge:sifting->frequency | sifting | frequency | data:sift_scores | 1_to_n | loose | Same SIFT file fans out to 7 population frequency jobs — data reuse |\n\n**Communication pattern**: All inter-task data exchange is via shared filesystem files (tar.gz archives and text files). No in-memory or streaming transfer observed.\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Workflow-Level Pattern\n\n### DAG Structure\n\n```\n[VCF input]       [SIFT annotation VCF]    [columns.txt]  [population files]\n     |                     |                    |                 |\n     v                     v                    |                 |\n individuals           sifting                  |                 |\n (n parallel/chr)    (1/chr, independent)       |                 |\n     |                     |                    |                 |\n     +------ (n_to_1) -----+--------------------+                 |\n                           |                    |                 |\n                    individuals_merge           |                 |\n                           |                   |                  |\n           +---------------+--------+          |                  |\n           | (1_to_n per chr x pop) |          |                  |\n           v                        v          |                  |\n    mutation_overlap            frequency  <---+------------------+\n    (chr x pop parallel)        (chr x pop parallel)\n           |                        |\n           v                        v\n    overlap_results          frequency_results\n```\n\n### Pattern Classification\n\n**Primary pattern**: scatter_gather + pipeline (hybrid)\n\n- **Scatter-gather**: `individuals` scatters a chromosome VCF into `n` parallel chunks; `individuals_merge` gathers them into one archive per chromosome.\n- **Pipeline**: Sequential stage chain: extract -> merge -> analyze. Analysis cannot start until both `individuals_merge` AND `sifting` complete for that chromosome.\n- **Embarrassingly parallel fan-out**: Both `mutation_overlap` and `frequency` run as independent grids (10 chr x 7 pop = 70 jobs each) with no inter-job dependencies within each task type.\n- **Broadcast fan-out**: `data:individuals_merged` and `data:sift_scores` are each read by multiple downstream consumers (1-to-n reuse).\n\nNo iteration or feedback loops. The DAG is strictly acyclic and forward-only.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: I/O Behavioral Hints\n\n| Concern | Location | Evidence |\n|---------|----------|----------|\n| small_file_overhead | individuals.py output | Each individuals job writes one file per individual inside tar.gz. With 2504 individuals x up to 250 parallel chunks, hundreds of thousands of small per-individual files are created before compression. Tar.gz wrapper mitigates staging cost but internal file count within each archive is very high. |\n| data_reuse | individuals_merge -> mutation_overlap and frequency | data:individuals_merged is independently extracted and re-read by both mutation_overlap and frequency for the same chromosome. data:sift_scores is also read by both. Up to 14 redundant reads per merged archive per chromosome (7 pop x 2 tasks). No shared cache between consumers. |\n| small_file_overhead | frequency.py output | 1000 bootstrap runs produce separate txt/png files per run per job. With 70 jobs (10 chr x 7 pop), total output can reach 70,000+ files before compression. 1000 PNG plots generated per job is particularly file-intensive. |\n| unnecessary_serialization | mutation_overlap.py, frequency.py | Both tasks independently extract and re-parse the same chr{c}n.tar.gz and SIFT text file. No shared in-memory representation between co-located tasks. [ASSUMPTION] Co-scheduling could allow data sharing but current implementation does not support it. |\n| partial_access | individuals.py | Each parallel individuals job reads only a specific line range of the VCF file. Code iterates lines sequentially with no byte-offset indexing, likely requiring scanning from the file start to reach the partition start line for each job. |\n| metadata_overhead | sifting.py | SIFT annotation VCF contains annotations for all variants but is filtered to a small fraction (only deleterious/tolerated variants with rs-numbers). Low concern -- one sequential scan per chromosome. |\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Summary and Cross-Reference Validation\n\n### Workflow Summary\n\n| Property | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| Workflow name | 1000genome |\n| Orchestrator | Pegasus (DAX/YAML via daxgen.py) |\n| Number of stages | 4 |\n| Number of task types | 5 |\n| Data granularity | Per-chromosome (10) x per-population (7) |\n| Max concurrency | 140+ jobs at analysis stage (70 overlap + 70 frequency) |\n| Primary pattern | scatter_gather + pipeline (hybrid) |\n| Data exchange | Shared filesystem (tar.gz and text files) |\n| Final output | 70 overlap archives + 70 frequency archives |\n\n### Cross-Reference Validation\n\n- All task inputs reference data objects defined in the registry. OK\n- All producer-consumer edges reference valid task and data IDs. OK\n- No deployment/scheduler/hardware details included in task descriptions. OK\n- sifting and individuals stages have no data dependency -- can run concurrently. OK\n- mutation_overlap and frequency have no data dependency on each other -- run concurrently. OK\n- 10 chromosomes confirmed from data.csv; 7 populations confirmed from data/populations/. OK\n\n### Unresolved / Unknown Items\n\n- **VCF line range access**: Whether sequential scanning from file start occurs for each parallel individuals job is `unknown` at the filesystem level; code evidence suggests sequential reads with no seek.\n- **Bash script equivalents**: daxgen.py supports a use_bash flag; bash equivalents assumed to have same I/O contract as Python scripts. [ASSUMPTION]\n- **Output filename suffix pattern** (e.g., `_s*`): Exact suffix values depend on runtime chromosome/population arguments, not fully determinable from static analysis alone. [ASSUMPTION: reflects runtime identifiers]\n"}}],"uuid":"30fd02c8-1783-4869-9469-54901d6c1578"}
